WEBVTT

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.940
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.820
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.660
but also in crime.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.780
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.490
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.260
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:49.610
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:54.990
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.740
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:08.080
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.920
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:19.930
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:24.180
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.190
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:33.280
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.280
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:42.490
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:48.790
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:55.130
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.100
Long Live CLAT

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:08.690
Shige, you're being sent to
New York City for the next two weeks.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.190
I humbly accept this duty.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.480
Say hello to Kanuka.

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:15.940
Yes, sir!

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:23.910
Mechanics, officers, and team members:
Take a look at this!

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.080
What?

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.790
What is it?

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:27.290
What's going on?

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:33.090
As rumored, I, Shigeo Shiba,
am being sent to New York!

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.590
Shige!

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.510
Are you all right?

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.510
I love New York...

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:45.680
Hey!

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.430
Shige!

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.780
You were moaning in your sleep.
Bad dreams?

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.700
Just stress.
I've been studying way too hard.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.870
First time in New York?

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:13.630
Actually, I'm being sent to help,
the new NYPD Labor Team!

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.000
They're using cutting-edge
technology.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.420
How long until we land?

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.380
We're circling now.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.370
NYPD Labor Team Headquarters.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.290
What's that?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.330
Huh? Haven't you heard
about the Labor Team?

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.210
No.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.710
For shame!
And you call yourself a driver!

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:58.250
You don't like the service?
Get out.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.170
Did you hear me? Get out.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:07.010
You certainly have a short fuse.
That's no way to get business.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.640
Why, back in Tokyo...

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:09.810
Get out.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.520
What...

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.440
are you doing?

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:20.360
Listen, banana boy:
Big-mouth twerps got a short life span.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.830
Remember the trade imbalance!

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:16.290
Kanuka...

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.710
I'm sorry, traffic was horrible.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:26.220
That's okay,
I wasn't expecting to be picked up.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.090
He really shook me up.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.180
I'm even more shaken up.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.260
More?

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.600
Yes, more.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.430
I can't believe
I'm really in America.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:41.230
Hey, what's up? The taxi driver
hadn't heard of your Labor team.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.110
You'll understand, soon enough.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:02.340
Did that Japanese travelogue
come in yet?

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.460
Do you have a membership card?

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.590
Uh, Kanuka...

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:06.260
Don't worry.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.880
The last booth on the end is open.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:17.640
Do we really need a travelogue?

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.140
Besides, that one's boring.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:20.730
Don't worry.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:23.980
Sit down.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:32.070
<i>Good evening, Lt. Clancy.</i>
<i>What is this week's password</i>?

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.240
The rain in Spain
falls mainly in the plain.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.040
<i>Password: Check. Voiceprint: Check.</i>

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.670
Pass

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.000
What is this?

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:56.770
<i>Thank you for using</i>
<i>the Manhattan Express.</i>

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.140
What's going on here?

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.060
We're here.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.860
CLAT?

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.200
Crime Labor Attack Team:
C-L-A-T, CLAT.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:18.200
This is our secret base,
90 meters beneath Hudson Bay.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:22.080
A secret base? CLAT is cool!

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:29.420
There are other entrances:
A theater, a cleaners, and so on.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:33.090
Only our inner circle knows the secret.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.390
We're an elite anti-terrorist force.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.020
Your team must be incredible!

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.360
This is cool!

00:07:58.950 --> 00:07:59.700
Just in time.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:06.290
This is the Japanese Labor engineer:
Shigeo Shiba.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:13.010
Thanks for coming. You must be tired,
so just take it easy today.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:17.760
But not too easy. We're going to
put you to work tomorrow.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:25.770
G-Block, Section 3: Prepare to mobilize.
Angel Team: Mobilize!

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:30.230
Prepare machines 1 and 2!
Open the gates!

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:33.110
I'll throw any dawdlers
into Hudson Bay!

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.260
Andante, standing by.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.430
Fortissimo, ready.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.240
Incredible!

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:20.410
Want to come along?

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:21.580
Of course!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.750
<i>Attention: CLAT is on the way!</i>

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:35.170
Wow, there's a CLAT
access gate here, too!

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:01.780
Situation?

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.450
Pretty bad!
We're fighting an Abraham.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.710
He's already trashed most of
the Energy Research Center.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:10.960
Yeah, looks bad.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.420
Captain, permission to fire?

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.880
Can't you come up with
anything better?

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.010
But he already trashed the place...

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:22.350
<i>And we want to keep</i>
<i>the damage minimal.</i>

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.260
<i>If you're really in doubt, then fire.</i>

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.810
But if we fire,
it not keep damage down.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:29.100
I see it.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.570
We see now! It come closer!

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:00.010
I warn you. We not keep damage down.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.840
Oh my God!

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.060
Stop or I'll shoot!

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.310
Not again!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.230
Why don't you like my
Hurricane Wave Punch?

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.100
He's getting away!

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.360
Don't bet on it!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:26.370
Target destroyed, but the criminal
escaped. Mop up for us.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:28.160
<i>Adam-12, roger.</i>

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.040
Let's head back.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:50.730
Good morning!

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:51.980
Good morning.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:53.690
Sleep well?

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:57.520
I think I'm still suffering from jet-lag.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:05.200
...and George says, "Don't cat fleas
bite humans, too?"

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:11.040
And I said, "George, you're thinking
of a scissor-bug!"

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.460
I don't get it.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:19.170
What's to get?
You got it, didn't you?

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:21.510
I know a good joke, too.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:26.970
Mister Bear said,
"I hate that fence over there."

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:32.140
Mister Bee said,
"Well I didn't picket."

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.780
I guess it loses something
in the translation.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.780
There's a report from
the commander.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.790
I have some good news,
and some extremely bad news.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:52.620
Start with whichever.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:57.040
To honor Mr. Shiba's visit
from Japan, today's lunch is sushi.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:57.500
Hooray!

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:02.460
And the bad news: The Abraham
last night was just a decoy.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.930
While the Abraham
created a diversion,

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:09.810
criminals in the Energy Research Lab
stole the Geo-Crystal.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:14.430
The crystal was already gone
by the time we arrived.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:20.150
Pardon me, but I'm new to CLAT.
What's a Geo-Crystal?

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:23.530
They've tapped the power
of the earth's core,

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:26.110
and stored it in the Geo-Crystal.

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:35.660
It's an incredible material
that is 99.8% efficient.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.540
Do you understand
the implications of that?

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:43.920
That amount of energy would dwarf
uranium or plutonium.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.510
It would be more powerful
than a hydrogen bomb!

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:55.230
The top brass are in a complete
and utter panic, so be ready.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.060
Roger.

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:57.310
As you were.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:13:59.690
Shige...

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:02.900
Mr. Godwood would like to see you.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.750
Oh, no! Why?

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.460
Why? Why?

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:43.570
In every country on Earth,
a bolt is a bolt, and a nut is a nut.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:46.360
Machines are honest.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.820
If you speak their language,
they'll never lie to you.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:54.280
Yes, Mr. Godwood.
My boss often says the same thing.

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:58.200
I'm sorry to drag you
halfway around the world.

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:01.880
We didn't really bring you here
for your technical skills.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.210
But...

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:04.750
But?

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:10.220
We have a small problem.
We can't make these blueprints work.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:12.680
This is...

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:16.100
Would you be willing
to help us on this?

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.680
Yes, sir! With pleasure!

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.730
Shige isn't back yet.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:25.190
The food is spoiling.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.070
Big waste.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:29.690
We should stick it in the refrigerator.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:31.740
It's probably too late.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:33.490
It's definitely too late.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:35.990
Even if he came back now...

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.700
His lunch is ruined.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:40.910
I assume a... clean-up is needed.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:52.470
The UN building is under attack
from a mysterious giant Labor!

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.730
Andante! Fortissimo!
Prepare to mobilize!

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:02.940
Shige!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.400
We did it, Kanuka.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:12.360
We skipped lunch to complete
the new scramble system.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:16.830
He's exhausted.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.700
Shige!

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:23.960
He's quite a man! Let's get him
to the infirmary, so he can rest.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:28.420
Mr. Godwood, please let me see
the launch with my own eyes.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.260
Take him to the control bridge!

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:33.380
Shige!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.470
Andante, standing by!

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.850
Fortissimo, ready!

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.810
Ingram, go!

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.650
Catapult room, stand by!

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.690
<i>Catapult room, stand by!</i>

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.250
Andante, heading out!

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:08.920
Fortissimo, heading out!

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:14.760
Incredible!

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.050
<i>That's just the beginning!</i>

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.510
Linear Catapult System: On!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:26.770
One, two, three G's!

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:29.150
Four G's! Five G's!

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:33.610
Under-Gate: Open!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.620
Shige Field: On!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.450
Shige Field: On!

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.250
This is incredible, Shige!

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:49.880
Our coefficient of friction
in water is dropping to zero!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:53.340
That's not all!
Godwood Drive: On!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:56.010
Godwood Drive: On!

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:30.080
What is that huge ugly Labor?

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.170
Something's wrong.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.960
I don't think it has a pilot!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:37.840
It's not a Labor, it's a robot!

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:39.510
It's moving!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:46.390
That's...

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:48.730
The Geo-Crystal!

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:06.370
The world must now bow down to <i>me!</i>

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:11.880
If you don't, I'll destroy the entire city
with my lovely Geo-Crystal!

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.920
One world, united under <i>me!</i>

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:19.170
Rubbish!

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.090
<i>Wait! Andante, support him!</i>

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:24.550
Support him? How are we
supposed to fight that thing?

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.510
Go, Mega-Iron!

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.020
Retreat!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.400
Andante, where's my support?

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:48.790
<i>Wait for me, you coward!</i>
<i>How can you abandon me, Captain</i>?

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:51.250
Can't this thing go any faster?

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:00.720
How dare you?

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:02.930
Mega-Iron, crush him!

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:12.520
What's wrong, Mega-Iron?

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:14.480
Hooray!

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.860
Serves you right!

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.570
Move, Mega-Iron! Move, I say!

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:36.500
You have the right to remain silent.

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:38.880
I must ask you
to come along peacefully.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:41.920
Fools!

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:50.270
A self-destruct system!

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:02.690
I'm sorry... this is just
too complex for me!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.110
I think I can handle it!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.160
If he fails...

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.620
North America will be wiped
from the map!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:11.620
Wow, major bummer!

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:17.080
Good luck, Mechanic of Japan!

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.350
God! Or Buddha!

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:36.810
Yes, I understand!

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:39.270
It's this!

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.440
You've just become
America's greatest hero!

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:46.740
They'll build a statue of you
right next to Lady Liberty!

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:51.160
Really? Little old me?

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:51.830
<i>Error: Tampering detected.</i>

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:08.510
Shige!

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.560
Oh, Mr. Godwood!

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:17.810
Why are you sleeping, you fool?

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:24.150
You fell down the stairs.
It'll take three weeks for you to heal.

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:26.820
You're so pathetic I could cry.

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:30.740
You can just forget about
that New York trip!

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:35.620
Don't feel too bad.
Just get better, soon.

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:37.660
I don't feel too bad.

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:41.830
I had a great dream!

00:23:00.730 --> 00:23:06.030
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:13.780
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:15.660
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:21.210
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:29.170
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:29.170 --> 00:23:30.880
I got it

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:38.430
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:44.310
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:45.860
One more chance

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:53.490
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:59.410
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:59.410 --> 00:24:03.500
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:12.840
This story is fiction...

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:12.840
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:21.020
Listen, there's going to be
a labor demonstration.

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:22.640
You trying to persuade me
to go too?

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:26.520
Nope, I hear there will be
Labors there we'll never get to try.

00:24:26.520 --> 00:24:28.190
You mean, the Self Defense Forces?

00:24:28.190 --> 00:24:32.610
Yes, I want those superior machines,
